# ── Semgrep scan scope (the gating "SAST (Semgrep)" job) ──────────────────────
# Excludes non-application surfaces from the app SAST gate. Application code under
# apps/*/ (routes, services, middleware, controllers, shared, utils) is STILL
# fully scanned — only the surfaces below are out of scope:
#
#   • Build / CI tooling — spawns child processes by design (running eslint/jest,
#     etc.); it is not a runtime attack surface, yet `detect-child-process` fires
#     on every scripts/ci/check-*.js.
#   • Test fixtures — deliberately use fixed/known test JWT secrets
#     (`jwt-hardcode`); not production credentials.
#   • Infra configs — nginx `.conf` files are reviewed by infra, not by a JS/TS
#     application SAST (`generic.nginx.*` header/proxy-host rules).
#
# Genuine application findings are fixed in code or annotated inline with a
# justified `// nosemgrep: <rule>` — never blanket-ignored here.

scripts/
**/__tests__/
**/*.test.js
**/*.spec.js
*.conf
